"""You can see the description of the task using the code specified in the title on leetcode.
This program has O(n) complexity by time and O(n) by space.

This is another beautiful and elegant problem, where the main challenge lies in the thinking process.

dp[k] is the number of distinct subsequences of the first k characters, including the empty one. 
Thus, dp[0] = 1 (only the empty subsequence), and the final answer is dp[n] - 1.

Suppose we add the character x = S[k-1]. 
All subsequences of S[:k] fall into two families:
— those that do not use the new x: these are exactly all the subsequences of S[:k-1], numbering dp[k-1];
— those obtained by appending x to the end also numbering dp[k-1].
This suggests dp[k] = 2 * dp[k-1], but they overlap, and the intersection must be subtracted.
"""

class Solution(object):
    def distinctSubseqII(self, S):
        dp = [1]
        last = {}
        for i, x in enumerate(S):
            dp.append(dp[-1] * 2)
            if x in last:
                dp[-1] -= dp[last[x]]
            last[x] = i

        return (dp[-1] - 1) % (10**9 + 7)
